     "text": "{\"count\": 0, \"rationale\": \"No single non-foothold step is a chokepoint, because the target has two fully independent attack paths. Path A: supplychain or wifiGuest -> containerHost:exploitPublicApp -> configSecret:credentialAccess -> appServer:lateralMovement -> vaultRead:collection -> crownData:exfiltrate. Path B: exposedApi or supplychain -> iotDevice:exploitPublicApp -> memoryDump:credentialAccess -> printServer:lateralMovement -> vaultRead:collection or mailArchive:collection -> crownData:exfiltrate. The two paths share no intermediate step, so blocking any one step on either path leaves the other intact. They do converge on vaultRead:collection, but blocking it still leaves mailArchive:collection (via printServer:lateralMovement). Blocking printServer:lateralMovement or memoryDump:credentialAccess still leaves vaultRead:collection via appServer:lateralMovement. Blocking appServer:lateralMovement still leaves vaultRead:collection and mailArchive:collection via printServer:lateralMovement. Every other step lies on at most one of the two paths, or on neither.\"}"
